# Tauri
src-tauri/target/

# Marrow (Phase 22): the source-relative boot mirror is transient recovery
# state written by `kernel_apply` and read by the pre-compile/pre-main guards.
# Never committed.
.loom-boot.json

# Test outputs
*.wav

# Rebirth (Phase 23): the genome bundle is a build output written by
# scripts/genome-bundle.mjs into the packaged app. Never committed.
src-tauri/genome/*
!src-tauri/genome/README.md

# The Cockpit is excised (Phase 23a). Nothing under public/ serves a deck,
# and Vite copies public/ verbatim into the binary — scratch left here ships.
public/decks/

# Rebirth (Phase 23): build.rs stages the TTS dylibs here from whichever
# profile is building, so tauri.conf can name one stable path. Build output.
src-tauri/libs/

# Rebirth (Phase 23): a dev threading ceremony writes this into the owner's
# own checkout. It points cargo at loomhome/vendor with `[net] offline = true`,
# so EVERY later cargo command in this checkout — LOOM's and the owner's —
# builds from the vendored crates and never reaches the network. It is
# machine-local (it names an absolute loomhome path) and PROTECTED in the
# genome; it is not the repository's to carry.
.cargo/config.toml
